    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We have developed a software toolkit, IRIPT (Integrated Urban Recycled Water Infrastructure Planning Toolkit) that facilitates planning and design of recycled water infrastructure for both non-potable and potable water reuse configurations incorporating satellite treatment plants (STPs).\r\n\r\nThe toolkit makes use of the six tools described below:\r\n- Pipeline Designer optimizes routing and sizing of pipelines for wastewater capture and recycled water distribution;\r\n- Selector assembles optimized wastewater treatment trains;\r\n- Calculator estimates fees, revenues, and subsidies to prepare a financial analysis for the recycled water owner;\r\n- Locator optimizes siting of STPs and associated wastewater diversions;\r\n- ToolIntegrator identifies a set of centralized and hybrid configurations that:\r\na) maximize recycled water supply\r\nb) maximize recycled water supply while also ensuring a financial benefit for the system owner\r\nc) maximize the net financial benefit for the system to its owner.\r\n- Analyst identifies a preferred configuration using decision-maker weights across a set of criteria, both financial and non-financial.\r\n\r\nWe apply IRIPT to case studies for the City of Golden, CO and Stanford / the City of Palo Alto, CA.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
